2. Collection
The first step is collecting indicators from trusted intelligence sources.
The collection process should record:
Indicator
Indicator type
Source
Timestamp
Confidence
Reputation
Expiration information
3. Validation
Not every indicator should automatically be trusted.
Before using a feed:
Check source reputation
Validate indicator format
Check indicator age
Remove duplicates
Check confidence level
Identify false positives
Verify whether the indicator is still active
More indicators do not automatically mean better security.
A low-quality feed can generate a large number of false positives.
4. Normalization
Different feeds may represent the same indicator in different formats.
Normalization converts them into a consistent format.
Example:
Source A:
192.0.2.10

Source B:
IP: 192.0.2.10

Source C:
indicator_type=ipv4
indicator=192.0.2.10
Normalized format:
Type: IPv4
Indicator: 192.0.2.10
Source: ThreatFeed
Confidence: High
First Seen: <timestamp>
Last Seen: <timestamp>
