8. Alerting
When an indicator matches internal telemetry, the security system can generate an alert.
A useful alert should provide:
Matched indicator
Source of intelligence
Confidence level
Affected host
User involved
Timestamp
Related events
Recommended investigation steps
Example:
Alert: Malicious IP Match

Indicator: 203.0.113.10
Type: IPv4
Confidence: High
Source: Threat Intelligence Feed
Host: WORKSTATION-01
Time: 10:32 UTC
Action: Investigate connection
9. Investigation
After an alert is generated, analysts investigate the event.
Important questions:
Which host contacted the indicator?
Which user was logged in?
When did the activity occur?
How frequently did the connection happen?
What process generated the connection?
Was data transferred?
Are there other affected systems?
Is the indicator associated with known malware or campaigns?
Investigation should combine threat intelligence with internal telemetry.
10. Automated Response
High-confidence indicators can be integrated into security controls.
Possible actions:
Block malicious IP addresses
Block malicious domains
Block malicious URLs
Quarantine malicious files
Isolate affected endpoints
Disable compromised accounts
Update proxy blocklists
Create firewall rules
Important
Automation should consider:
Confidence
Indicator age
False-positive risk
Business impact
Expiration time
Avoid blindly blocking every indicator.
11. STIX
STIX — Structured Threat Information Expression
STIX provides a standardized way to represent and share threat intelligence.
It can describe:
Indicators
Malware
Threat actors
Campaigns
Attack patterns
Relationships
Observed data
STIX = Standard way to represent threat intelligence
12. TAXII
TAXII — Trusted Automated Exchange of Intelligence Information
TAXII provides a standardized mechanism for exchanging threat intelligence between systems.
STIX = How threat intelligence is represented

TAXII = How threat intelligence is exchanged
Together:
       STIX
        ↓
Threat Intelligence Format
        ↓
       TAXII
        ↓
Threat Intelligence Exchange
